The desk merged every date report into #4471 and marked it known: one parser bug, one fix queued. The export's own cause logic splits those reports. Intake tags are a guess from the browser. Cause follows the tenant (locale and booking form).

<CauseTable ticket={4471} />

<Callout kind="warn">
#4471 owns the parser cause. The hint cause has no desk ticket of its own. Subject-line merge (decision 0001) put both in one pile.
</Callout>

## The two problems

**parser.** The shared parser reads every date month first. Day-first tenants get a flipped month and day. This is the cause most of #4471 shares.

**hint.** booking-v3 prints `MM/DD/YYYY` under the date field. People type month first, as the hint says. The form still reads the tenant's day-first order. That is not the parser.

Five reports in the parser pile were read as a one-day move. They stay in the parser count because cause is by tenant. They are footnoted on the table, not a third cause.

## Tickets filed

